# Licensing of the patches in this directory

SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later

Every `*.patch` file here modifies Wine source code, so each is a derivative work
of Wine and is licensed under the **GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1
or (at your option) any later version** — the same terms as Wine itself.

That is deliberate, not incidental: it is what allows these changes to be sent to
the Wine project or to CodeWeavers, and combined with Wine or with CrossOver's
published Wine sources, without a licence conflict.

The canonical LGPL-2.1 text is not duplicated here. It ships with Wine as
`COPYING.LIB` in any Wine source tree (including CodeWeavers' published
`crossover-sources-*.tar.gz`), and is published at
<https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html>.

The MIT licence in the repository root applies to the tooling (`bin/`, `tools/`,
`docs/`, `profiles/`) and explicitly does **not** apply to this directory.

## Third-party material in this directory

Two files are **not our work**. They are diffs of CodeWeavers' published CrossOver
Wine sources, kept here as reference material while investigating differences
between that tree and upstream Wine:

- `crossover26-wined3d.diff`
- `crossover26-winemac.drv.diff`

They are Copyright © CodeWeavers, Inc. and contributors, LGPL-2.1-or-later, and
are redistributed here under those terms. Do not treat them as changes authored by
this project, and do not assume the MIT licence covers them.

`dxmt-0001-include-iomanip.patch` modifies DXMT, which carries its own licence;
see that project.

## Subdirectories

- `retracted/` — patches that were **wrong** and were replaced by a better
  approach. Kept so the mistake is visible. Same LGPL terms.
- `superseded/` — patches that were **right** but are no longer needed, because the
  base (CrossOver's Wine) already carries the fix. Same LGPL terms. Three of them
  are ports of CodeWeavers' own hacks and are credited as such in that README.
